#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:5 8b304ab1b717411fb21e60f212ca0c7b
msgid "Archived: DJI F330 FlameWheel QuadCopter Assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:7 9a844db62a864b53bcc50ac93d8752a8
msgid ""
"This article provides and overview of the DJI F330 FlameWheel QuadCopter,"
" and instructions for how it may be assembled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:11
#: c44a0720f1c143f2845fe04a652ba2d3
msgid "The DJI F330 FlameWheel is inexpensive, sturdy and small."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:13
#: 01f88a322a9e44b6bec4362cfe77890c
msgid "It can be flown indoors or out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:14
#: 9fdc2380cfc64dc399cbf8a5c4f65836
msgid ""
"Even though it is compact, the F330 is substantial and can easily carry a"
" battery that will permit 15 minute flights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:16
#: bf3b2db1822b4ec387491caf904a9192
msgid "The F330 can carry a GoPro type camera or FPV system if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:17
#: 55cfce78c70a4f29ac6c43f3440f49f1
msgid ""
"The ARF (Almost Ready to Fly) kit is a super bargain and includes motors,"
" ESCs (Electronic Speed Controls) and Propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:19
#: 5e058e552f1440a18c96d82e4deaf5bc
msgid ""
"The DJI Motors and ESCs provided in the ARF kit are of high quality, very"
" durable and long lasting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:21
#: 21ba06555a7f4bbb8007eb6c5859ece5
msgid ""
"The frame is extremely rugged and all replacement parts are readily "
"available and inexpensive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:25
#: 6cf7da61b3204e16a1c4e5862b7e9005
msgid "The DJI F450 Flamewheel is an excellent larger alternative to the F330"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:27
#: d5ccea4399c34b758b0385d9e25278ff
msgid ""
"The F450 FlameWheel ARF kit has a larger frame, 30 amp ESCs and 10\" "
"props for only $10.00 more than the F330."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:29
#: 706b50089c8345369a1a4cba8e67733c
msgid ""
"The F450 is well suited to carrying a GoPro camera, brushless gimbal, "
"landing gear and a larger battery for longer flights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:31
#: 46b969d66d264e669b0182c127a38788
msgid ""
"The F330 and F450 FlameWheel are excellent platforms for the PX4 and "
"PixHawk autopilots as well as the APM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:34
#: 3eefd4e1187c4ec1a4bcbfaa4feb4dc3
msgid ""
"I  have, in fact, converted my personal F330 to use the PX4 autopilot "
"with great success."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:36
#: a84e85cce3ef481a887a082de2c3082d
msgid ""
"I strongly recommend the F330 and F450 ARF kits, they are reliable, "
"rugged and inexpensive and are suitable for many uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:39
#: 92b3c3a56dbd465e8f3013fd278979d7
msgid ""
"The quality is excellent, the components provide long trouble free "
"service, and replacement parts are cheap and available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:41
#: 74339ba378ff4c978143fc6a0296e772
msgid ""
"I genuinely don't think you can find a better deal in an APM / PX4 / "
"Pixhawk compatible MultiCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:45
#: c935b6e03d1243e58c8a100a3873c542
msgid "Components required in addition to the Flamewheel ARF kit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:47
#: 44ba3823fd084529bceaa52208eeeff5
msgid ""
"An autopilot (APM 2.6, PX4FMU + PX4IO or Pixhawk) with UBlox GPS module "
"and power supply module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:49
#: 6782fd7169bf4756952e30db455bd699
msgid ""
"RC equipment: RC transmitter and a 5+ channel radio receiver (PPM-SUM "
"compatible for PX4 or Pixhawk)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:51
#: 05e3baee9bfe4f67a9913e8d1cd59eb0
msgid ""
"A 3 cell 1800mah to 2650mah LiPo battery and an appropriate battery "
"Charger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:53
#: 5616ba1abc6e4d49acdd45a5cf59557f
msgid ""
"Miscellaneous: female to female 3 wire receiver / servo cables, a battery"
" strap, tie wraps and some assorted hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:55
#: 1a50dd03561f4142936a02bcfb2a16d6
msgid ""
"You will also need an adjustable soldering iron, rosin cored solder, blue"
" thread locker and some small Metric Allen wrenches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:62
#: c7e744b0c4a34966bbc857e27f3caebd
msgid "Frame and Motor Assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:64
#: 1a267a8de46e4aeabe7ceb88a922b322
msgid ""
"Get the \"manual\": `F330_User_Manual_v1.6_en.pdf "
"<http://dl.djicdn.com/downloads/flamewheel/en/F330_User_Manual_v1.6_en.pdf>`__."
" (If there is a more recent version, you may find it in the `DJI website "
"Flamewheel support section <https://www.dji.com/flame-wheel-"
"arf/download>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:68
#: 5c72a40a2ae94f04a5723eb628ba81b5
msgid ""
"It is more of an assembly diagram than a manual, but the pictures are "
"definitely useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:71
#: 770127a8f94a423bbedc8ea0d9cf43ff
msgid ""
"The DJI instructions show soldering the ESCs to the Power Distribution "
"Board (bottom frame plate) first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:74
#: ab2022e2840b4f70bf3ba767ed9e4979
msgid ""
"In our example they were put in after frame assembly because it makes it "
"possible to fit things more closely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:76
#: 7399a4c305a34fbf8580ce6b9b8c4fb7
msgid ""
"But it does require a bit of creativity when soldering the ESC leads to "
"the bottom plate / power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:78
#: 5ea4493b2d0348e6802a0652f60e9764
msgid "Your choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:80
#: 251be949684d42ac9c05f189d6b85ae3
msgid ""
"Use Blue or purple removable thread locker very sparingly on the threads "
"of the Allen screws when you assemble the frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:83
#: 2c5de712699f449ea871646b3ac76a80
msgid ""
"Try to keep excess thread locker off of the plastic. This is not actually"
" achievable, but do the best you can."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:86
#: 384c424935584af5bd73504a5325d49c
msgid ""
"Motor and frame screws have a shoulder on them and you need to tighten "
"them all sufficiently so that the shoulder fully seats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:89
#: 9075f72941f946f6b9a0d18e0b3d35c1
msgid ""
"A good method is to install all screws (with Locktite) loosely then "
"tighten all the screws on each frame arm one at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:91
#: 01cc3269c9d647e49250aa328e8f48bd
msgid "Do this in one sitting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:93
#: cb3a02baa3644bd8b9b307420b6de9fb
msgid ""
"When installing the motors, pre-bend the motor leads upward where they "
"exit the motor bottom so that the motor can sit flat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:96
#: 2e72acbb06f44d2c9fa868a28457855b
msgid "Have the leads exit towards the center of the copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:97
#: a7f99d0d57104e8aa3ce16a17dd182ab
msgid ""
"Motor bottom screws are off set and it can only be installed 2 ways, "
"toward the center is correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:98
#: 7daa4e67d9944a308a4eadeca05f80da
msgid ""
"The motor screws are short and it is tricky to start the first screw on "
"the motor bottom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:99
#: 70315cb5577648e684769cf21c2814a7
msgid "Ensure that the motor leads are not pushing the motor up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:100
#: c5d7a0951b3e4f5681a48300c1710a71
msgid ""
"Use blue Locktite on each screw and install all 4 screws for a motor "
"loosely and then tighten them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:102
#: c070f9c89d1d41d7b75b69c7b4881244
msgid "Thread the motor leads down through the first 2 large frame member holes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:104
#: 36950a85aff44d91800c4d07079defc1
msgid "Or you can run them around the frame member if you prefer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:109
#: 6dbb76e261844817bcfc9971a7d9721a
msgid ""
"Be careful to wire motors to the PixHawk using the ArduPilot numbering "
"convention for QuadX below. The numbering convention in the DJI "
"FlameWheel F450 instructions are different, and incorrect writing leads "
"to attitude instability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:117
#: 1721337b5fb44b2cbdb7b72d78e5dde3
msgid "ESC Installation and Soldering the Power Distribution Board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:119
#: ac74f8d72e6045d78f3f7224d6ca93c6
msgid "Install the ESCs with tie wraps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:121
#: 36e7e27011a141fc9dd23f29eefc0dfb
msgid ""
"Thread the Tie Wraps from front to back through the frame members and "
"between the motor bullet connector sockets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:122
#: fb04a91cf22a47d0b942d03e9c9bc885
msgid ""
"Install the ESC power leads through the slot under the bottom of the "
"frame member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:123
#: 293e2d8519754781bb4b113a8d3b1f56
msgid "Then trim and solder them to the power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:124
#: e2c39bd34c5042c190a73594e4a463c0
msgid ""
"This is a little harder than going around the outside of the frame but is"
" neater and provides a little more battery clearance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:126
#: 30cba72556ab46a6b8d131926b50997a
msgid ""
"The above illustration shows a power distribution \"Y\" connector which "
"functions the same as the FlameWheel's built in power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:128
#: 316a820a89894ed08a8f5bb02db8f23e
msgid ""
"When you solder the ESC and Battery power leads to the power distribution"
" board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:130
#: 62c114fd401d47c6b39bd263d0506d8d
msgid ""
"Flux and preheat both the pads and the wire in order to get a properly "
"tinned (wet) solder joint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:131
#: ff998c784ac84cc992b258c436046e15
msgid ""
"The board can soak up quite a bit of heat so set your soldering iron "
"sufficiently hot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:133
#: c27b54a45961427cb3d35cb19f9636f6
msgid ""
"The DJI ARF FlameWheel kits have Opto ESCs which do not include a BEC so "
"you will need an external power supply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:135
#: 62253eaa39814fdea04a1baaee2643e8
msgid ""
"The APM, PX4 and Pixhawk are now available with a power supply you can "
"use, other wise you will need to buy a BEC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:136
#: c9e72c4f832a44cb9d6e84bdbca2c3c4
msgid ""
"Castle Creations makes an excellent and very reliable 10/5 amp BEC for "
"about $20.00."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:137
#: 3ff4b27bdd784675981b4e9baa6353b3
msgid ""
"Use a switching BEC in any case, they are more reliable and a lot more "
"efficient than linear ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:139
#: fb70ef1e1947418781f67f125c630568
msgid ""
"You do not need to and in fact can't balance the DJI ESCs as shown "
"elsewhere in the Copter Wiki."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:141
#: a9a53c6457b545ba8ccd669dc9a28b11
msgid ""
"DJI ESCs are digital, optically isolated, are completely pre-balanced at "
"the factory and work fine out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:147
#: 3e29364d047545668b6498c6b71dc6cf
msgid "Reduced Vibration Installation of the Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:149
#: 295a9bd2c5b34e219645052adb00f2f0
msgid ""
"The autopilots require special attention be paid to removing as much "
"vibration from the autopilot as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:152
#: a7761ff4810e41ae93d2e86b56107597
msgid ""
"This F330 FlameWheel has a special anti-vibration suspension mounting of "
"the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:154
#: 1fdf97d930b44eceba95fc63ec7aa4ed
msgid ""
"It uses a folded over 1/16\" O-ring at each corner of the autopilot "
"around a screw sticking out of a small standoff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:155
#: 26a123695c39463f89f7a9734a5fdfc1
msgid ""
"If you choose to use this method leave 1/10\" to 1/8\" clearance from "
"each board corner for proper short coupled spacing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:157
#: 7d8c5b933b7a48bd9a8e9ab01c3fd83b
msgid ""
"The F330 requires minor surgery with a Dremel tool on each frame arm to "
"achieve proper hole spacing in the top plate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:160
#: 5d172173b0e3482a8a2d33742c3a07c1
msgid ""
"Kyosho Zeal Gel is an easy to install and fully satisfactory alternative "
"to the O-ring suspension method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:163
#: 168ae3c0dc894ead8183b1a14c0ad26d
msgid ""
"Simply put a 3/4 inch square of adhesive backed Kyosho Zeal Gel under "
"each corner of the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:165
#: f07fe82ea91c4b4bbe58915b14a82779
msgid ""
"And secure the autopilot with a Velcro strap over 1/2\" of soft foam in "
"light tension. (Do NOT over tighten!)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:168
#: 8c4882582b1f4b5a98e4fc453d721edf
msgid ""
"Either the Kyosho Zeal Gel or the O-ring suspension method will allow you"
" to limit vibration to about 1/10 G which is fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:170
#: bfb430d998314fad80dcf2cb4e346273
msgid ""
"Anti-vibration techniques, methods and \"tuning\" are covered in greater "
"detail in the :ref:`Anti-Vibration section of the Wiki <common-vibration-"
"damping>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:172
#: e5c32e36d48a4a53984870f1979b6990
msgid ""
"Compensation for compass interference from the motors is :ref:`covered "
"here! <common-magnetic-interference>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:173
#: 2fe6c62fcabf410cbcfa89db39f5869a
msgid ""
"Correct wiring of the autopilot and configuration for flight are covered "
"extensively elsewhere in the Wiki."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:181
#: 4cc66ba6f9cc428c899eb85aa25c6c6a
msgid ""
"\\*The Velcro on the board and frame above is not in use and is not "
"actually touching\\*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:185
#: 6c170272fe4941979b6cfa6d376101b6
msgid "Getting Ready to Fly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:187
#: 8c96cd9e051e46c481c7f7f1536ed63d
msgid ""
"Our construction method allows the battery to be inserted between the two"
" frame plates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:190
#: abbebd59d70940179cd54aa957bef5ba
msgid "This is an optimal location regarding the QuadCopter's center of gravity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:192
#: 39ace17c442c4973a27ad089f67cc479
msgid ""
"The 2650mah LiPo Turnigy Nano battery used here is as large as will "
"comfortably fit, but it will permit 15 minute plus flights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:194
#: 2fdfb737881647a0aad218d1fb753f85
msgid ""
"Cover bottom frame power distribution solder joints with liquid "
"electrical tape or silicone to prepare for the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:196
#: 6969be5f7f7c4c6b8036e04a94cf96c9
msgid ""
"Wrap the battery in bubble wrap and tape it in place to provide "
"additional electrical isolation from the solder joints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:198
#: 4ea5a6fbca1149f899cc216a21ddfdc3
msgid ""
"This will also provide cushioning from vibration and sub-optimal "
"\"landings\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:200
#: 94e5250058024868a7c55247c8f482ee
msgid ""
"Use a Velcro battery strap through the frames bottom slots to retain the "
"battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:203
#: 731e13afd6f24a1f9deac0d2fbdf4442
msgid "The stock 8\" DJI props that are supplied with the F330 ARF kit work fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:206
#: 75a24014eb7d46df9ca8053c2e644539
msgid ""
"However the F330 FlameWheel can definitely benefit from a 9\" prop (10\" "
"will not fit on the F330)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:208
#: 8b73afb1cac44858a8e3bbee9185f6bd
msgid ""
"GemFan 9\" multirotor \"Carbon Filled\" props are only $2.00 each and are"
" superior to the stock 8\" props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:210
#: fa175e3b9fe24fd7a773841508c21c5d
msgid ""
"These GemFans are almost impossible to break and the 9\" ones are "
"considerably more efficient than the stock 8\" props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:212
#: 8615631db87342c9a9c7f2a3188f4522
msgid "9\" GemFan propellers are not made to fit the oval hubs of the DJI Motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:214
#: 757bcc988afa49fe9147bd66e87ae7d8
msgid ""
"But you can carefully bore them out to about .31\" with an ordinary drill"
" and they will fit perfectly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:216
#: 5917c85fbd9847f6aeeae1abe162b71d
msgid ""
"On My F450 Flamewheel, I use 11\" GemFan propellers bored out the same "
"way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:218
#: 43766aac7ed749d396abdf570cb0b48b
msgid ""
"Generally a larger prop diameter is better so long as you don't exceed "
"motor or ESC maximums or cause over heating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:220
#: 17dc596839b143298415217ff48c7a1c
msgid ""
"Make sure the propellers are right side up (printing on top), this won't "
"fly worth a damn if they are upside down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:223
#: 50dda2a7bf644b6396c535443f2d6986
msgid ""
"The ESCs and motors automatically disarm after 10 seconds without the "
"motor turning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:226
#: 747a11b2742b4695a92bee9a322f9a53
msgid ""
"So anytime you have remained stationary (on the ground) for over 10 "
"seconds you will need to rearm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:228
#: 8117da6aebcf4fab972f78b9d425c0aa
msgid "This is an excellent safety feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:230
#: f9165ffa2f3a4916a44fbe82a5e9a199
msgid ""
"You will need to Install Mission Planner software on your PC as "
"instructed elsewhere in this Wiki."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:233
#: 0e3d7f228f1e48d7b4c1983a9f343879
msgid ""
"You will then need to use Mission Planner to load the QuadCopter firmware"
" to your autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:235
#: 7927d8962d374c52a1210c3f8d395abf
msgid ""
"And you will then need to set up various flight parameters for your "
"FlameWheel in the Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:237
#: a08a0e4becea413e84d160bf4f9024f6
msgid ""
"(Do Not Attempt to Calibrate the DJI Opto ESCs and Do Not install the "
"propellers until directed to do so)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:240
#: 5d63c3ee81f94a46a756c774f782fe2d
msgid ""
"To prepare to fly place your copter on your takeoff location, turn your "
"transmitter on and plug in the copter's battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:243
#: 8c7c90323fb64015add4bb6bf0416aec
msgid ""
"(If you have a PX4 or Pixhawk autopilot depress the start button for five"
" seconds)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:245
#: 3d6aebc8d3cf425898d478095a695947
msgid "The ESC's should emit a short series of musical notes and then be quiet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:247
#: 77652ba222b54b249c1000caf5e9c930
msgid ""
"You are then ready to arm by holding the throttle stick down and to the "
"right for 5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:249
#: c3edc7b0ecbd4c6494f5614bfd82f674
msgid ""
"After arming you must throttle up the motors within 10 seconds or you "
"will need to re-arm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:251
#: 273beaecfccd44f6b36da7f29dc87831
msgid ""
"When you are done flying disarm by holding the throttle down and to the "
"left for 5 seconds and disconnect the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:253
#: b7c34a4949d2494ba4ebdf2b403af650
msgid ""
"A good set of initial PIDs for flying the FlameWheel F330 or F450 in "
"Stabilize Mode (as of Copter version 3.0.1) are:"
